#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
patch_L322_D_6_gallery_builder_pole_20260924.py -- L-322 Stage D, gallery
patch 1 of 3: the cache builder serves Earth's pole and tilt of date.

Built on gallery d037929110878de85a172ce955c15f24d2298902 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/tonyquintanilla.github.io, from
orrery fb8d927e1581f6ad2fe49aa04a8d30d50e7f8d71 at
https://github.com/tonylquintanilla/palomas_orrery (the geometry it copies
and the two real Horizons days it tests against).

WHAT IT DOES

    The cache builder fetches, on every build, Earth's north pole for the
    day (Horizons observer quantity 32, target 399) and the Earth-Moon
    barycenter's orbit (target 3 about the Sun), works out Earth's tilt
    between them, and serves all three as pole_of_date in
    data/solar-system/coverage_index.json with their source blocks. It
    also serves frame_constants: kilometres per AU and the frame's angle,
    read from data/constants_export.json, for the page to read in patch 2
    instead of typing them. Before a swap it recomputes the tilt from what
    it is about to serve, and refuses the swap (#P) if they disagree. A
    pole that cannot be fetched never stops a build.

    The page does not read any of this yet; it draws exactly as before
    until patch 2.

FILES

    changed  tools/gallery_cache_builder.py
    changed  tools/test_gallery_cache_builder_offline.py
    changed  data/objects_config.json   (one block on Earth; no numbers)
    changed  gallery_maintenance_run.py (runs the new test)
    new      tools/pole_of_date.py      (the tilt geometry, from the orrery)
    new      tools/test_pole_of_date.py

    Permanent: the two new files, the builder's new functions, and the
    config block. This script itself is one-shot; archive it to
    documentation/ once it has run.

RUN COMMAND

    Save this file in the gallery repo root (the folder holding
    interactive.html), open it in VS Code, and click Run. Or:
        python patch_L322_D_6_gallery_builder_pole_20260924.py

    Success: one "ok" line per edit and per new file, then
    "PATCH APPLIED", then the next steps.
    Failure: "FAILURE: ..." and NOTHING is written. Undo after a success
    is Discard Changes in GitHub Desktop.

Written September 24, 2026 with Anthropic's Claude Opus 5.5.
"""

